APXF["fr-saumur"] = lo({ lede: "The appellation of the tuffeau limestone around Saumur, for whites, reds, rosés and, above all, sparkling wine aged in the area's caves.", cat: "AOC, red, white, rosé and sparkling; Saumur Puy-Notre-Dame for red", rec: "1936 (modified 2016)", facts: [["Area", "About 2,200 ha"], ["Colors", "Sparkling 65%, white 17%, red 15%, rosé 3%"], ["Grapes", "White: Chenin. Red: Cabernet Franc, Cabernet Sauvignon, Pineau d'Aunis. Sparkling: Chenin, Chardonnay, Cabernet Franc and others"]], place: "Saumur sits on tuffeau, a soft, porous chalky limestone quarried for centuries to build the Loire châteaux, leaving hundreds of kilometers of caves now used for ageing wine and growing mushrooms. Saumur Puy-Notre-Dame, a red-only zone in the south of the appellation, was recognized as a separate name.", rules: "All styles; traditional-method sparkling Saumur (Saumur Fines Bulles or Mousseux) is the largest share, from houses such as Bouvet-Ladubay, Gratien et Meyer and Ackerman. White Saumur is Chenin; red is mainly Cabernet Franc.", glass: "Taut, mineral Chenin, notably from Brézé, whose whites were once prized above many Burgundies; supple Cabernet Franc; fresh sparkling wine.", producers: ["Domaine Guiberteau", "Château Yvonne", "Domaine des Roches Neuves", "Clos Rougeard (Saumur Blanc and Brézé)", "Bouvet-Ladubay", "Langlois-Château", "Château de Brézé"] });
APXF["fr-saumur-champigny"] = lo({ lede: "The red Cabernet Franc appellation east of Saumur, the most famous red of the middle Loire, with Clos Rougeard as its legend.", cat: "AOC, red only", rec: "1957 (modified 2011)", facts: [["Area", "About 1,400 ha"], ["Grapes", "Cabernet Franc (at least 85%), Cabernet Sauvignon, Pineau d'Aunis"]], place: "The appellation covers nine communes on the tuffeau plateau and slopes east of Saumur, along the Loire, around the village of Champigny.", rules: "Red only, mostly from Cabernet Franc. The cooperative of Saint-Cyr-en-Bourg, with cellars dug in the tuffeau, makes a large share.", glass: "Fresh, perfumed Cabernet Franc with raspberry, violet and a chalky texture; the best, such as Clos Rougeard, age for decades.", producers: ["Clos Rougeard", "Domaine des Roches Neuves", "Château du Hureau", "Domaine Filliatreau", "Château de Villeneuve", "Domaine Antoine Sanzay"] });
