APXF["fr-chinon"] = lo({ lede: "The leading red appellation of Touraine, around Rabelais's town on the Vienne, for Cabernet Franc from gravel, sand and tuffeau slopes.", cat: "AOC, red, rosé and white", rec: "1937 (modified 2016)", facts: [["Area", "About 2,400 ha"], ["Colors", "Red 87%, rosé 8%, white 5%"], ["Grapes", "Red and rosé: Cabernet Franc (Cabernet Sauvignon allowed in small amounts). White: Chenin"]], place: "Chinon lies on the Vienne just before it joins the Loire. Wines from the sandy and gravelly river terraces are light and early; those from the tuffeau and clay-limestone slopes (coteaux) are firm and long-lived. François Rabelais was born nearby and praised the wine.", rules: "Mostly red from Cabernet Franc, locally called Breton; a little Chenin white.", glass: "Fresh, red-fruited Cabernet Franc with graphite and herbal notes; slope wines from producers such as Charles Joguet and Baudry age for decades.", producers: ["Domaine Bernard Baudry", "Domaine Charles Joguet", "Domaine Olga Raffault", "Couly-Dutheil", "Philippe Alliet", "Domaine de la Noblaie"] });
