APXF["fr-vouvray"] = lo({ lede: "The great Chenin Blanc appellation east of Tours, on tuffeau cliffs above the Loire, making every style from dry to sweet and sparkling.", cat: "AOC, white only: still (sec to moelleux) and sparkling", rec: "1936 (modified 2011)", facts: [["Area", "About 2,200 ha"], ["Styles", "Sparkling 52%, still 48%"], ["Grapes", "Chenin Blanc; Orbois (Arbois) up to 5%"]], place: "Vouvray's vineyards sit on the plateau above tuffeau cliffs on the right bank of the Loire, on clay with flint (perruches) and clay-limestone (aubuis). Wines are aged in caves cut into the tuffeau.", rules: "White only. The style depends on the vintage: sec, demi-sec, moelleux and sparkling (mousseux or pétillant). Cool years go to sparkling, warm years to sweeter wines.", glass: "Chenin with quince, apple, honey and chalk, and high acidity that lets even dry wines age for decades; Huet's sweet wines from Le Haut-Lieu, Le Mont and Clos du Bourg are among France's greatest.", producers: ["Domaine Huet", "Domaine François Pinon", "Domaine du Clos Naudin (Foreau)", "Domaine Vincent Carême", "Domaine Sébastien Brunet", "Domaine Champalou"] });
