// ===== Centre-Loire =====
APXF["fr-sancerre"] = lo({ lede: "The world's benchmark for Sauvignon Blanc, from the chalk, limestone and flint hills around a hilltop town on the upper Loire.", cat: "AOC, white, red and rosé", rec: "1936 for white; 1959 for red and rosé (modified 2011)", facts: [["Area", "About 3,000 ha"], ["Colors", "White 84%, red 10%, rosé 6%"], ["Grapes", "White: Sauvignon Blanc. Red and rosé: Pinot Noir"]], place: "Sancerre's 14 communes lie on the left bank of the Loire, opposite Pouilly. Three soils matter: terres blanches, Kimmeridgian marl like Chablis's, in the west (around Chavignol); caillottes, stony Portlandian limestone; and silex, flint clay near the river (around Saint-Satur and Ménétréol). Chavignol is also home to Crottin de Chavignol goat cheese.", rules: "White from Sauvignon Blanc; red and rosé from Pinot Noir. Village and lieu-dit names such as Chavignol, Bué, Les Monts Damnés and La Côte des Monts Damnés often appear on labels.", glass: "Crisp, citrus, gooseberry and flint, with chalky minerality; silex wines are smoky and taut, terres blanches fuller. Red Sancerre is light Pinot Noir.", producers: ["Domaine Vacheron", "Domaine François Cotat", "Domaine Pascal Cotat", "Domaine Alphonse Mellot", "Domaine Henri Bourgeois", "Domaine Gérard Boulay", "Domaine Lucien Crochet", "Domaine Vincent Pinard"] });
APXF["fr-pouilly-fume"] = lo({ lede: "Sauvignon Blanc from the right bank of the Loire opposite Sancerre, around Pouilly-sur-Loire, with a reputation for smoky flint.", cat: "AOC, white only", rec: "1937 (modified 2011)", facts: [["Area", "About 1,400 ha"], ["Grape", "Sauvignon Blanc (called Blanc Fumé locally)"]], place: "The vineyards lie on Kimmeridgian marl, limestone and flint around Pouilly-sur-Loire and Saint-Andelain. The 'fumé' is usually explained by the smoky aroma from flint or by the grey bloom on ripe Sauvignon grapes.", rules: "White Sauvignon only. Didier Dagueneau's ambitious wines, notably Silex and Pur Sang, raised its profile in the 1990s and 2000s.", glass: "Fuller and more smoky than many Sancerres, with citrus, gooseberry and flint.", producers: ["Domaine Didier Dagueneau", "Château de Tracy", "Domaine Jonathan Pabiot", "Domaine Alexandre Bain", "Château du Nozet (de Ladoucette)", "Domaine Serge Dagueneau"] });
APXF["fr-pouilly-sur-loire"] = lo({ lede: "A tiny appellation for Chasselas around Pouilly, the remnant of a vineyard that once supplied Paris with table grapes.", cat: "AOC, white only", rec: "1937 (modified 2011)", facts: [["Area", "About 30 ha"], ["Grape", "Chasselas"]], place: "Same zone as Pouilly-Fumé.", rules: "White from Chasselas only; Sauvignon from the same land is Pouilly-Fumé.", glass: "Soft, light, neutral white.", producers: ["Domaine Serge Dagueneau"] });
